ening a possible loophole in black-hole arguments against global symmetries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0089"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:19c9c1e6fba4b2bbc51e5f93c908910bdc2dc5da0390fd0db4c6d02d450e228c","title":"Can the circle-reduced effective-action symmetry under derivative-corrected Buscher transformations be extended from tree level to higher genus, reproducing nonzero one-loop interactions known from S-matrix calculations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0091"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:19d7266b3d2936d31b4717919302be76edd15431d270e7b9632c8210378eaa95","title":"How do uniform, non-uniform and localized string stars compete in canonical and microcanonical ensembles when a large spatial circle is added, and when do quartic corrections change their phase diagrams?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:19d57fcafc0f3cc6feaf25d5e104395c3763beaa85489569c2cedec3d97c0194","title":"How does a free shift reduce the duality group of asymmetric type-IIB orbifolds, and what light towers, supersymmetry enhancements and decompactified theories occur at the additional infinite-distance cusps?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0095"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:19971072e711635d8f078b183d6ebf73d0c892bd3ddea33c74a59825df47e6a5","title":"Can generalized calibrations protect non-supersymmetric type-II AdS vacua against D-brane bubble decay, including abelian bound states, and establish classical stability of D-branes already present in a background?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0095"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:19a07933894f5e403f5920005c538134a11056af0a041ba24f4962dabaef770c","title":"Can a proposed chiral spectrum for the n